    "answer": {
      "short": "$AL\\approx13.8\\text{ km}$ and $BL\\approx10.7\\text{ km}$.\n\nUse the bearings to obtain interior angles $50^\\circ$, $100^\\circ$ and $30^\\circ$, then apply the sine rule.",
      "worked": "The bearing of $B$ from $A$ is $215^\\circ$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\angle BAL&=215^\\circ-165^\\circ\\\\\\angle BAL&=50^\\circ\\\\\\angle ABL&=135^\\circ-35^\\circ\\\\\\angle ABL&=100^\\circ\\\\\\angle ALB&=180^\\circ-50^\\circ-100^\\circ\\\\\\angle ALB&=30^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\n\nUse the sine rule in $\\triangle ABL$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{AL}{\\sin100^\\circ}&=\\frac{7}{\\sin30^\\circ}\\\\AL&=\\frac{7\\sin100^\\circ}{\\sin30^\\circ}\\\\AL&\\approx13.8\\text{ km}\\\\\\frac{BL}{\\sin50^\\circ}&=\\frac{7}{\\sin30^\\circ}\\\\BL&=\\frac{7\\sin50^\\circ}{\\sin30^\\circ}\\\\BL&\\approx10.7\\text{ km}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
